1
00:00:29,820 --> 00:00:30,780
Paradise

2
00:00:58,680 --> 00:01:01,840
that's the target I'm waiting for you,

3
00:01:02,100 --> 00:01:03,880
I'm not going to

4
00:01:30,800 --> 00:01:33,677
I tried to talk to others into
giving Ken a second chance,

5
00:01:33,760 --> 00:01:35,597
but no, they wouldn't go for it.

6
00:01:35,680 --> 00:01:36,757
They don't trust him.

7
00:01:36,840 --> 00:01:38,137
I'll tell you who I don't trust.

8
00:01:38,220 --> 00:01:42,417
That crazy white-haired lady Palmon saw
doing something freaky to a control spider.

9
00:01:42,500 --> 00:01:46,677
She turned it into Golemon, and he tried
to destroy a dam and flood the local town.

10
00:01:46,760 --> 00:01:48,737
That's what I call a bad attitude.

11
00:01:48,820 --> 00:01:51,517
Our Digimon were fighting the
good white, but it wasn't enough.

12
00:01:51,600 --> 00:01:53,977
You'll leave in like it when
Mimi and I called Ken for help,

13
00:01:54,060 --> 00:01:56,797
but when she finally admitted to
herself that she was wrong about Ken,

14
00:01:56,880 --> 00:01:59,117
Hawkmon digivaled into his champion form,

15
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:00,030
Aquilamon.

16
00:02:00,113 --> 00:02:01,864
I didn't know he had it in him.

17
00:02:04,240 --> 00:02:05,220
Juggles Shinka.

18
00:02:06,140 --> 00:02:07,669
Iman, I'm one of my heart.

19
00:02:10,640 --> 00:02:11,470
Ow!

20
00:02:11,700 --> 00:02:13,818
Sure, Iman, watch what you're doing.

21
00:02:13,960 --> 00:02:15,666
You don't have to yell at me.

22
00:02:17,760 --> 00:02:19,460
He's right. We need a rest.

23
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:20,960
I'm with you.

24
00:02:23,620 --> 00:02:25,197
Do you have any wishes yet?

25
00:02:25,280 --> 00:02:29,809
Kari, I wonder, do you think it's possible
that Ken's in some kind of danger?

26
00:02:30,100 --> 00:02:31,100
What do you mean?

27
00:02:31,280 --> 00:02:34,757
That woman that Palmon was telling us
about, I just know that she's up to no good,

28
00:02:34,840 --> 00:02:36,899
and I think he might be in her way.

29
00:02:38,500 --> 00:02:40,206
Look on the bright side, Ken.

30
00:02:40,460 --> 00:02:43,166
At least no one will
ever say you think small.

31
00:02:43,680 --> 00:02:45,640
You certainly have a good point.

32
00:02:46,280 --> 00:02:47,500
Just trying to help.

33
00:02:48,760 --> 00:02:49,997
Don't touch it, it's...

34
00:02:50,080 --> 00:02:51,100
Pure evil.

35
00:02:51,940 --> 00:02:53,540
They're my creation.

36
00:02:54,380 --> 00:02:57,737
But even I don't understand
how Aru Kunemon can take one

37
00:02:57,820 --> 00:03:01,200
of my control spires and
somehow turn it into a Digimon.

38
00:03:01,640 --> 00:03:02,897
I don't get it, Wormon.

39
00:03:02,980 --> 00:03:05,717
When I was the Digimon Emperor,
I understood this sort of thing,

40
00:03:05,800 --> 00:03:07,657
but nothing makes sense to me now.

41
00:03:07,740 --> 00:03:08,640
Earth to Ken?

42
00:03:08,960 --> 00:03:09,901
You're a genius.

43
00:03:10,020 --> 00:03:11,537
I'm sure you'll figure it out.

44
00:03:11,620 --> 00:03:12,450
Thanks, pal.

45
00:03:12,533 --> 00:03:14,594
I'm glad someone still has faith in me.

46
00:03:15,460 --> 00:03:17,437
Now I just have to have faith in myself.

47
00:03:17,520 --> 00:03:19,337
Since I was the one
who built these things,

48
00:03:19,420 --> 00:03:21,777
you'd think I would have some
kind of clue as to how they work.

49
00:03:21,860 --> 00:03:23,960
I don't. I don't.

50
00:03:24,800 --> 00:03:27,120
As the Digimon Emperor, I was a genius.

51
00:03:27,360 --> 00:03:28,831
Now I'm just playing kin.

52
00:03:29,380 --> 00:03:30,321
That's a relief.

53
00:03:30,580 --> 00:03:31,937
Yeah, as far as you're concerned.

54
00:03:32,020 --> 00:03:33,961
But what about the digital world?

55
00:03:35,480 --> 00:03:36,700
They'll get over it.

56
00:03:38,580 --> 00:03:42,109
Wormon, looking at these things
makes me sick to my stomach.

57
00:03:42,800 --> 00:03:43,630
Oh, great.

58
00:03:43,860 --> 00:03:46,197
Stick your head between your
knees and take a deep breath.

59
00:03:46,280 --> 00:03:47,986
This whole thing is my fault.

60
00:03:49,280 --> 00:03:52,868
Oh, how many times do I have to
tell you it's not your fault?

61
00:03:53,060 --> 00:03:55,737
There are people you can
talk to about this stuff.

62
00:03:55,820 --> 00:03:59,097
And why didn't you talk to them
before becoming the Digimon Emperor?

63
00:03:59,180 --> 00:04:01,997
It had to be easier than
building control spires.

64
00:04:02,080 --> 00:04:03,668
Excellent question, Wormon.

65
00:04:04,520 --> 00:04:05,397
Hmm, all right.

66
00:04:05,480 --> 00:04:09,377
If you can't figure out how they work,
then I'll just have to knock them all down.

67
00:04:09,460 --> 00:04:10,880
It seems sturdy enough.

68
00:04:11,100 --> 00:04:12,220
Of course it is.

69
00:04:12,840 --> 00:04:14,497
What do you mean by that anyway?

70
00:04:14,580 --> 00:04:15,997
Don't you think I know what I'm doing?

71
00:04:16,080 --> 00:04:16,937
You said it.

72
00:04:17,020 --> 00:04:19,726
Yeah, even if it is what
we were all thinking.

73
00:04:20,160 --> 00:04:22,237
Hey, that rock slide
thing wasn't my fault.

74
00:04:22,320 --> 00:04:23,237
It was Flamedermond.

75
00:04:23,320 --> 00:04:24,150
Was not.

76
00:04:24,233 --> 00:04:25,063
Was too. Was not.

77
00:04:25,146 --> 00:04:25,976
Was too.

78
00:04:26,059 --> 00:04:26,889
Was not.

79
00:04:26,972 --> 00:04:27,802
Was too.

80
00:04:27,885 --> 00:04:28,715
Those meddling kids.

81
00:04:28,800 --> 00:04:32,329
Just when I had the DigiWorld
so deliciously destroyed, too.

82
00:04:33,800 --> 00:04:34,630
What's this?

83
00:04:34,713 --> 00:04:35,620
A split end?

84
00:04:37,800 --> 00:04:39,260
How did this happen?

85
00:04:40,400 --> 00:04:41,230
Intolerable.

86
00:04:42,180 --> 00:04:43,680
Oh, that's enough.

87
00:04:44,160 --> 00:04:45,680
Now it's personal.

88
00:04:48,840 --> 00:04:49,880
Spirit Needle!

89
00:05:00,320 --> 00:05:01,150
Go.

90
00:05:01,233 --> 00:05:02,533
That bridge offends me.

91
00:05:05,800 --> 00:05:07,817
But you said give me
the rock on the bottom.

92
00:05:07,900 --> 00:05:08,730
Did not!

93
00:05:09,320 --> 00:05:10,150
Huh?

94
00:05:10,233 --> 00:05:11,637
What does he think he's doing?

95
00:05:11,720 --> 00:05:13,257
Looks like he's headed for the bridge.

96
00:05:13,340 --> 00:05:15,737
Maybe he's just admiring
the detailed architecture.

97
00:05:15,820 --> 00:05:20,120
Yeah, or a way to blow
it up. No! Not again!

98
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:21,830
Davis!

99
00:05:22,700 --> 00:05:23,530
Yeah!

100
00:05:24,460 --> 00:05:25,290
Digimon!

101
00:05:28,600 --> 00:05:29,430
Digimon!

102
00:05:30,220 --> 00:05:31,050
Digimon!

103
00:05:33,160 --> 00:05:35,060
Armor! Digimon!

104
00:05:35,960 --> 00:05:36,790
Raidromon!

105
00:05:36,873 --> 00:05:38,272
The Storm of Friendship!

106
00:05:39,280 --> 00:05:40,440
Earthquake Drill!

107
00:05:41,680 --> 00:05:44,717
Minotaromon is a champion
Digimon with a nasty left jab.

108
00:05:44,800 --> 00:05:48,624
This earthquake drill will turn
that bridge into stepping stones.

109
00:05:49,780 --> 00:05:51,800
Not my bridge! Get him!

110
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:53,830
Thunderfly!

111
00:05:58,180 --> 00:05:59,010
Davis!

112
00:05:59,093 --> 00:06:00,100
Taking a swim?

113
00:06:00,340 --> 00:06:02,600
Very funny, TP. A little help here?

114
00:06:03,960 --> 00:06:06,260
Davis is gonna mess this up again!

115
00:06:06,900 --> 00:06:07,730
Pokémon!

116
00:06:07,813 --> 00:06:08,660
My pleasure!

117
00:06:10,960 --> 00:06:12,840
Pokémon Digimon 2!

118
00:06:15,900 --> 00:06:16,730
Aquilamon!

119
00:06:19,680 --> 00:06:20,720
That's enough!

120
00:06:25,960 --> 00:06:28,200
My bay! Hold on!

121
00:06:28,580 --> 00:06:30,286
That thing's a control spire!

122
00:06:31,020 --> 00:06:32,420
It's not real!

123
00:06:32,660 --> 00:06:34,560
It's real enough! Let's get him!

124
00:06:34,900 --> 00:06:35,960
You got it!

125
00:06:37,020 --> 00:06:38,120
You ready?

126
00:06:38,940 --> 00:06:39,770
Digimon!

127
00:06:39,940 --> 00:06:41,797
Digi-Armor Energize!

128
00:06:41,880 --> 00:06:45,480
Tokomon, Armored Digivolts 2!

129
00:06:45,680 --> 00:06:47,980
Hanuman, Armored Digivolts 2!

130
00:06:53,420 --> 00:06:55,900
Devimon, Angel of Light!

131
00:07:00,540 --> 00:07:02,800
Pegasmon, Flying Hope!

132
00:07:03,720 --> 00:07:04,600
Thunderblast!

133
00:07:12,820 --> 00:07:14,860
Ah, now you're talking? Huh?

134
00:07:17,180 --> 00:07:18,120
Oh, no!

135
00:07:18,480 --> 00:07:20,833
Looks like he took a big bite out of it.

136
00:07:21,580 --> 00:07:23,940
Aw, I feel so violated.

137
00:07:24,300 --> 00:07:25,680
We still respect you.

138
00:07:25,820 --> 00:07:26,877
That's right, Davis.

139
00:07:26,960 --> 00:07:28,657
We're just gonna have to rebuild it again.

140
00:07:28,740 --> 00:07:30,257
And it'll be easier this time.

141
00:07:30,340 --> 00:07:31,317
She's right, you know.

142
00:07:31,400 --> 00:07:33,857
We really learned a lot
from all our mistakes.

143
00:07:33,940 --> 00:07:37,528
Yeah, and this will give you
the chance to make new mistakes.

144
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:40,500
Aw, but I liked my old mistakes better.

145
00:07:41,020 --> 00:07:41,850
Huh?

146
00:07:42,800 --> 00:07:45,197
Hey, speaking of mistakes,
we should ask Ken to help.

147
00:07:45,280 --> 00:07:46,517
Are you out of your mind?

148
00:07:46,600 --> 00:07:47,837
Thanks for the support.

149
00:07:47,920 --> 00:07:50,717
Seriously, I bet he'd jump
at the chance to help us.

150
00:07:50,800 --> 00:07:51,700
I don't know.

151
00:07:52,060 --> 00:07:53,320
I don't trust him.

152
00:07:54,340 --> 00:07:57,458
You may be right, but he's
the only one who can help.

153
00:07:58,240 --> 00:08:00,720
Well, I'm just not comfortable around him.

154
00:08:01,040 --> 00:08:03,077
It's hard for people to really change.

155
00:08:03,160 --> 00:08:04,513
I think it's too risky.

156
00:08:04,900 --> 00:08:08,371
You got a point, but I have a
good feeling about him, Cody.

157
00:08:08,700 --> 00:08:09,530
Really?

158
00:08:09,613 --> 00:08:10,620
But why, Davis?

159
00:08:12,120 --> 00:08:13,280
The Digi-Egg.

160
00:08:13,400 --> 00:08:16,457
If you had seen what I saw,
you'd believe in him, too.

161
00:08:16,540 --> 00:08:20,220
I mean, his crest of kindness
turned into a golden Digi-Egg.

162
00:08:20,400 --> 00:08:22,165
It was the most amazing thing.

163
00:08:22,360 --> 00:08:24,177
You're going to think I'm
crazy when I say this,

164
00:08:24,260 --> 00:08:26,737
but I guess you already think
I'm crazy, so here goes.

165
00:08:26,820 --> 00:08:28,557
That Digi-Egg believed in him,

166
00:08:28,640 --> 00:08:31,897
and it was like it was telling
me I could believe in him, too.

167
00:08:31,980 --> 00:08:35,880
It almost felt like it was asking
me to go ahead and trust him.

168
00:08:36,180 --> 00:08:39,397
I know that's not very logical,
but then again, neither am I.

169
00:08:39,480 --> 00:08:43,017
All I know is he has to have the
Crest of Kindness for a reason.

170
00:08:43,100 --> 00:08:44,688
And what about his Digimon?

171
00:08:44,800 --> 00:08:46,197
He believes in him, too.

172
00:08:46,280 --> 00:08:48,877
I think it's because Wormmon
knew it was in his heart.

173
00:08:48,960 --> 00:08:49,790
He's good.

174
00:08:49,873 --> 00:08:50,703
I know it.

175
00:08:50,786 --> 00:08:51,737
But what if you're wrong, Davis?

176
00:08:51,820 --> 00:08:54,837
And besides, he's made it clear he
doesn't want to be part of our team.

177
00:08:54,920 --> 00:08:56,920
Yeah, I know, but I'm an optimist.

178
00:08:57,360 --> 00:09:00,837
Goody for you, but realistically,
he could still be bad to the bone.

179
00:09:00,920 --> 00:09:02,177
I think Cody is right.

180
00:09:02,260 --> 00:09:03,120
He usually is.

181
00:09:05,040 --> 00:09:08,137
I'm bored, and all this talk
isn't getting us anywhere.

182
00:09:08,220 --> 00:09:10,637
Don't forget, that crazy white-haired
chick is still out there,

183
00:09:10,720 --> 00:09:12,132
and she's up to no good.

184
00:09:14,440 --> 00:09:15,270
What's that?

185
00:09:16,500 --> 00:09:18,100
It's a message from Izzy.

186
00:09:18,580 --> 00:09:20,700
I'm getting a real bizarre signal.

187
00:09:20,980 --> 00:09:22,377
It's not too far from you.

188
00:09:22,460 --> 00:09:23,290
Check it out.

189
00:09:23,440 --> 00:09:26,397
Hey, it looks like the sector
where Ken's base went down.

190
00:09:26,480 --> 00:09:27,480
Let's get moving.

191
00:09:33,520 --> 00:09:35,137
Ready to take a break, Stingmon?

192
00:09:35,220 --> 00:09:37,926
I guess I've wreaked
enough havoc for one day.

193
00:09:38,180 --> 00:09:39,160
I want a bath.

194
00:09:39,480 --> 00:09:41,517
No offense, but you really need one.

195
00:09:41,600 --> 00:09:42,953
Please, Ken, slow down.

196
00:09:43,120 --> 00:09:44,917
I have awfully short legs, you know.

197
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:49,257
And not to put too fine a point on it,
these spires you built have splinters.

198
00:09:49,340 --> 00:09:52,217
Sorry, Wyrmon, this isn't exactly
sundae in the park, is it?

199
00:09:52,300 --> 00:09:53,597
No, that's a great idea.

200
00:09:53,680 --> 00:09:55,277
You see, you're still a genius.

201
00:09:55,360 --> 00:09:57,277
Let's have ice cream sundaes in the park.

202
00:09:57,360 --> 00:10:00,637
That does sound good, but would you
settle for half a jelly roll at home?

203
00:10:00,720 --> 00:10:01,550
Yummy.

204
00:10:08,480 --> 00:10:12,997
what's going on can you tell my theory is
that a major power source is about to melt

205
00:10:13,080 --> 00:10:15,237
down if you guys don't
shut it down and i mean

206
00:10:15,320 --> 00:10:17,849
fast it'll explode what
do you mean explode

207
00:10:18,160 --> 00:10:23,020
i mean explode you know boom
this is bad but what can we do

208
00:10:24,660 --> 00:10:29,117
oh the crest of kindness i'll bet it's
because ken's crest isn't there anymore

209
00:10:29,200 --> 00:10:34,540
i don't care what anyone says we need
ken's help and we need it now but davis

210
00:10:35,240 --> 00:10:36,917
Shouldn't we talk about this?

211
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:37,860
We just did.

212
00:10:38,340 --> 00:10:40,357
You guys are going to
have to trust me on this.

213
00:10:40,440 --> 00:10:43,087
I know I'm right and we
don't have much time.

214
00:11:00,060 --> 00:11:00,890
Hey, Ken.

215
00:11:01,720 --> 00:11:03,397
I feel queasy. Me too.

216
00:11:03,480 --> 00:11:05,137
Let's save the rest for later.

217
00:11:05,220 --> 00:11:06,050
What's wrong?

218
00:11:07,380 --> 00:11:08,560
My, my, my.

219
00:11:08,760 --> 00:11:10,760
Now, isn't this just too domestic?

220
00:11:11,680 --> 00:11:12,520
You again.

221
00:11:13,100 --> 00:11:15,480
Oh, please, Ken, don't talk to her.

222
00:11:15,980 --> 00:11:17,451
Did I come at a bad time?

223
00:11:17,600 --> 00:11:20,480
Well, I'll be going. Bye-bye. No, wait.

224
00:11:21,660 --> 00:11:24,077
Your little friend there
is being quite rude.

225
00:11:24,160 --> 00:11:24,990
Why should I?

226
00:11:25,200 --> 00:11:27,197
Because you're the one
who keeps calling me.

227
00:11:27,280 --> 00:11:28,751
What do you want with me?

228
00:11:29,420 --> 00:11:32,037
What makes you think I want
anything from you, maybe?

229
00:11:32,120 --> 00:11:33,857
Then why are you bothering me?

230
00:11:33,940 --> 00:11:36,517
What do you plan to do
to the digital world?

231
00:11:36,600 --> 00:11:39,260
Why, Ken, what a nosy little boy you are.

232
00:11:39,400 --> 00:11:42,165
That's really none of
your business, now is it?

233
00:11:43,360 --> 00:11:44,500
This is crazy.

234
00:11:44,680 --> 00:11:46,557
What do you expect us to do, Davis?

235
00:11:46,640 --> 00:11:48,020
Ah, where's Ken?

236
00:11:48,420 --> 00:11:51,457
When he was the Emperor, we
were always tripping over him.

237
00:11:51,540 --> 00:11:52,937
Of course it's my business.

238
00:11:53,020 --> 00:11:55,120
You're using my control spires.

239
00:11:57,200 --> 00:11:58,080
My creep.

240
00:11:59,120 --> 00:11:59,950
Asian.

241
00:12:00,140 --> 00:12:00,970
My shame.

242
00:12:01,053 --> 00:12:04,980
You think rather well of
yourself, little boy emperor

243
00:12:06,420 --> 00:12:07,460
Poor me,

244
00:12:07,700 --> 00:12:12,157
why did I do such awful things When I
could have used my awesome powers for good

245
00:12:12,240 --> 00:12:15,760
Telephone, oh Ken Oh
yes, you're so special

246
00:12:16,920 --> 00:12:17,750
What,

247
